      {
        "id": 2586567780,
        "content": "I've investigated this, and this happens because there is [logic](https://github.com/ubiquity-os-marketplace/command-start-stop/blob/b3405d795416687afbeb080092dce2c7b33111c1/src/plugin.ts#L23) associated to `pull_request.edited`. This was implemented because if you first open a PR without linking the issue, then edit your pull-request to add `Resolves #--` we need to listen for this event to properly assign a user. I suppose the fix would be to assign the author of the pull-request instead of the user who edited it.",
